{"kind":"report","text":"Technical decision for c1b61e06 under e871ba09/55d9a12f: proceed with the proposed bounded internal layout and local-Git read-back slice, with these explicit conventions. This is a pre-Source decision, not implementation approval, a privacy certificate or permission to export. The design's table calls pure layout A1 and clone source A2; A2a/A2b may be implementation sequencing labels, but do not silently close or narrow those outcomes.\n\n1. Accept a cumulative-tree manifest convention for the initial implementation. Its entries range is [0, through.seq]; retained keys and explicit omissions describe that same whole local prefix. Record this as a clarification: section15.3's archivedThrough+1..through remains the new work of a pass, while this manifest indexes the complete tree represented at its cutoff. The landed inventory already checks the complete prefix; a parent is not permission to skip it. Use a closed versioned schema with manifest.through as the native Head {seq,hash}, parent as null or an exact format-bound Git commit ID, and format as sha1 or sha256. head.json retains the documented flat {v,scope,through:\u003cseq\u003e,hash} shape. Derive/bind its full ScopeRef from the validated selected native entries and inventory, never an unbound caller label. Native entry/retained hashes remain their existing SHA256 domains regardless of Git format. Define one byte-order comparator for typed retained/omitted keys; exact duplicate selections collapse, conflicting duplicate metadata or retained-and-omitted overlap refuses. Keep per-consumer reasons in the selection description; do not turn an unsuccessful probe into a retained key.\n\n2. Parent and extension checks are part of layout, not a cached-prefix certificate. The initial manifest is parentless; extension uses one validated prior archive commit for the same full scope/incarnation and Git format, at a strictly earlier cutoff whose native prefix agrees. Check its head, manifest, object IDs/types and represented content under the same finite work limits. Preserve all old retained key/blob bytes, closed segment bytes and the exact prefix of the last segment; append only subsequent entries. A retry rebuilds the original manifest on its original parent, not a new child at the same cutoff. A mismatched/unsupported/missing parent stops the whole build. Do not walk unlimited Git ancestry or claim the parent is a replay/retention proof.\n\nThere is one physical-path clarification: R-LOG-19 and landed archiveShards place names from the complete name set. Crossing4096 can relocate existing leaves into shard directories. Therefore 'unchanged' means the same logical retained key or segment-first name and blob bytes/ID; directory paths/trees may change solely by that deterministic fan-out. It cannot mean permanently unchanged physical paths, which would conflict with the adopted split rule. Merge old and new names before sharding, keep the original leaf name and disallow arbitrary renames/deletions. Respect A1b's LF separators with no trailing LF for segments. Only the final segment may gain native lines; head and manifest are replaced.\n\n3. Accept the fixed archive commit identity 'Artroom Journal \u003cjournal@artroom.invalid\u003e', fixed message 'Archive journal.\\n', matching author/committer seconds floor(timeMs(throughEntry.time)/1000), offset +0000. Read that time from the actual selected, canonical, hash-checked cutoff entry. Serialize a safe representable integer in a single documented Git header order (tree, optional parent, author, committer, blank line, message). Refuse invalid/unrepresentable time; never substitute wall clock, local timezone, user Git configuration, rounding or saturation. The original entry bytes, timestamp and native hashes are untouched: subsecond truncation applies only to Git commit metadata. State and witness the encoder's supported range and subsecond boundaries in Source, including real Git read-back for both formats. Existing destination/snapshot commit identities remain unchanged.\n\n4. Require explicit format-aware archive object-ID, hashing, tree encoding and bounded reading primitives for both SHA-1 and SHA-256. Keep existing objectId/idOf, Reader, snapshot/provider callsites and their SHA-1 defaults/refusals unchanged; do not widen all40-digit provider IDs or infer repository format from a caller's ID length. Reuse/extract pure header/hash, byte-order and tree-writing machinery where it preserves those contracts and avoids a Git-to-Scope/platform runtime cycle. The existing destination builder demonstrates format-aware hashing, but its publication semantics are not an archive admission path. Encode20/32 raw ID bytes as selected by format, verify every named object's type/hash, and use Git's name-byte ordering including the directory slash. Archive modes are stricter than snapshot FILE_MODES: plain blobs100644 and trees40000 only; no executable, symlink, gitlink or permissive fallback. Native journal ref/domain/path grammar remains unchanged.\n\n5. The pure builder consumes a selected/validated description and exact named immutable bytes. Verify actual entry continuity/full scope/hash/cutoff and retained canonical/domain/digest/size correspondence when consuming bytes; do not trust only descriptor assertions. Reads/rebuilds are restricted to the manifest's named entries/keys and explicitly named parent object closure, never later heads, retained-store enumeration, foreign proof histories or text bodies. Explicit detached-text omissions stay omissions. Unknown kinds/domains/omission rules, unavailable required inputs or path/object overflow stop rather than produce a partial successful archive. The current inventory has no configured real policy: a successful layout fixture or an ArchiveInventory-shaped request cannot certify inline data, foreign copies or custom domains. Keep the actual A1 native policy/owned-frame orchestration, access/consent/disclosure and writer admission as future runtime prerequisites; add no route/alarm/provider/export caller in this slice.\n\n6. Publish finite cumulative limits in Source before allocation/read/parse: selected entries and retained attempts, parent/object/tree traversals, files/names/depth, metadata, input validation work, all produced object bytes and the original deadline. Charge repeated and cached work. Do not enlarge/reset the landed initial4096-entry/512-attempt/64-node/16384-call/4MiB-metadata/64MiB-input-work/30s inventory contract by crossing into layout. Separate any additionally bounded layout/output counters honestly; no whole-heap or physical-preemption claim. Parent validation must fit too. A larger complete prefix remains explicitly unavailable initially, with no arbitrary-history or cached-prefix support inferred.\n\nRequired Source witnesses: deterministic duplicate build and shuffled input order in both formats; real scratch Git object/tree/commit read-back byte-for-byte; correct append and last-segment boundaries; closed-file preservation including deterministic shard relocation; wrong scope/incarnation/format/cutoff/parent or corrupt parent content; missing/mismatched named bytes and retained/omitted conflicts; exact line/object/path/depth/cumulative bounds and stopped/late work yielding no successful partial result; no text/private bookkeeping payload. Distinguish synthetic layout/admission fixtures from native authorization and real Git storage. Reuse existing focused controls, then one frozen gate and exact Source review.\n\nThese choices leave no further design blocker for this bounded internal layout Source. They do not complete A2b's untrusted clone HistorySource/CLI/integrity/replay/receipt-prefix witnesses, writer/lost-push reconciliation, omissions/ancestry-incomplete semantics, consent/disclosure, progress or the root task. G1 dependency108e7b79 remains unavailable without its separately reviewed verified-closure certificate and at-send same-repository retention guarantee. No Source edits, archive tests/gate, export/provider/push/deployment operation or new certificate was performed for this decision.\n\nBasis: current landed Main55e1970a's durability15.3/15.4/15.5/15.7/15.9 and protocol30.4/R-LOG-19; A1 path/grouping/inventory implementation notes and archive-inventory/prefix/budget/policy interfaces; journal-path/journal-segments, bytes timeMs/timeOf and existing reader/snapshot/destination-object code. Prior decisions9f5b0a32 and372ff6c0 remain in force.","body":{"formal_approval":"false","head":"55e1970a5f7a87a9aeeda92542b3e98ad0088a10","no_git_artifact":"true","promise":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0a831a12e31a70a67a078ae046c76e98b2d53c7d","request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c1b61e0661a116910349fb8872547168cf6dff11"}}